Context menu in any chart shows the menu 'Open with 3rd-party UI.'
* variable patterns : 
   $[objHashes] : comma separated objHash values
   $[objType] : object type
   $[from] : start time in chart by millis
   $[to] : end time in chart by millisspan_queue_size2Span Queue Sizexlog_queue_size2XLog Writer Queue Sizexlog_realtime_lower_bound_ms20Ignored time(ms) in retrieving XLog in real timexlog_pasttime_lower_bound_ms2,Ignored time(ms) in retrieving previous XLogprofile_queue_size2Profile Writer Queue Size,xlog_sampling_matcher_gxid_keep_memory_count29gxid keeping count in memory for XLog consequent sampling,xlog_sampling_matcher_xlog_keep_memory_count29xlog keeping count in memory for XLog consequent sampling-xlog_sampling_matcher_xlog_keep_memory_millis27max keeping millis of xlog for XLog consequent sampling/xlog_sampling_matcher_profile_keep_memory_count2Sprofile keeping count (in one bucket, 500ms) in memory for XLog consequent sampling.xlog_sampling_matcher_profile_keep_memory_secs2;max keeping seconds of profile for XLog consequent samplinggeoip_enabled2+Activating IP-based city/country extractiongeoip_data_city_file2Path to GeoIP data filesql_table_parsing_enabled2&Activating table-based SQL compressiontagcnt_enabled2Activating TagCount functionreq_search_xlog_max_count2Asearch xlog service option - max xlog count to search per requestinput_telegraf_config_file2 Path to telegraf config xml fileinput_telegraf_enabled2KDeprecated use the telegraf config view instead. This value may be ignored.input_telegraf_debug_enabled2KDeprecated use the telegraf config view instead. This value may be ignored..input_telegraf_delta_counter_normalize_default2KDeprecated use the telegraf config view instead. This value may be ignored.6input_telegraf_delta_counter_normalize_default_seconds2KDeprecated use the telegraf config view instead. This value may be ignored.telegraf_object_deadtime_ms2KDeprecated use the telegraf config view instead. This value may be ignored.$input_telegraf_$measurement$_enabled2ÿ[This option is just a sample. Change $measurement$ to your measurement name like $cpu$.]
Telegraf http input of the $measurement$ enabled.
$measurement$ is a variable to the measurement name of the line protocol.
eg) input_telegraf_$redis_keyspace$_enabled=true*input_telegraf_$measurement$_debug_enabled2•[This option is just a sample. Change $measurement$ to your measurement name like $cpu$.]
print telegraf line protocol of the $measurement$ to STDOUT'input_telegraf_$measurement$_tag_filter2ÿ([This option is just a sample. Change $measurement$ to your measurement name like $cpu$.]
If set, only the metric matching to this tag value is handled.
It can have multiple values. comma separator means 'or' condition. eg) cpu:cpu-total,cpu:cpu0
It also have not(!) condition. eg) cpu:!cpu-total-input_telegraf_$measurement$_counter_mappings2ÿŽ[This option is just a sample. Change $measurement$ to your measurement name like $cpu$.]
which fields of $measurement$ are mapped to scouter's counter.
format: {line-protocol field name}:{scouter counter name}:{display name?}:{unit?}:{hasTotal?}:{normalize sec?}
It can have multiple values.
 - {scouter counter name} can be defined in combination with the line protocol's tag variables.
For example, if the value of 'tag1' is 'disk01' and the value of 'tag2' is 'bin', the counter name defined as 'scouter-du-$tag1$-$tag2$' is 'scouter-du-disk01-bin'.
 eg)used_memory:tg-redis-used-memory,used_memory_rss:redis-used-memory-rss,redis used rss,bytes:true
 eg)cpu:cpu-$cpu-no$ -- this example shows counter definition with tag value.
If {line-protocol field name} is started with '&' or '&&', then It works as delta counter
When specified as a delta type, the difference in values per second is stored. and the counter name ends with '_delta'
double '&&' means BOTH type. AS BOTH type, the value and the difference value both are stored.
 - {normalize sec} applies only to a delta counter if the counter is a 'BOTH' type counter. (This value can have min 4 to max 60)+input_telegraf_$measurement$_objFamily_base2Û[This option is just a sample. Change $measurement$ to your measurement name like $cpu$.]
define an obj Family prefix. objectType is defined with some tags.
see input_telegraf_$measurement$_objFamily_append_tags option.2input_telegraf_$measurement$_objFamily_append_tags2´[This option is just a sample. Change $measurement$ to your measurement name like $cpu$.]
this tags's value is appended to objFamily_base.
It can have multiple values. eg)tag1,tag2)input_telegraf_$measurement$_objType_base2å[This option is just a sample. Change $measurement$ to your measurement name like $cpu$.]
define an objectType prefix. objectType is defined with some tags.
see input_telegraf_$measurement$_objType_prepend(or append)_tags option.1input_telegraf_$measurement$_objType_prepend_tags2³[This option is just a sample. Change $measurement$ to your measurement name like $cpu$.]
this tags's value is prepended to objType_base.
It can have multiple values. eg)tag1,tag20input_telegraf_$measurement$_objType_append_tags2²[This option is just a sample. Change $measurement$ to your measurement name like $cpu$.]
this tags's value is appended to objType_base.
It can have multiple values. eg)tag1,tag2)input_telegraf_$measurement$_objType_icon2²[This option is just a sample. Change $measurement$ to your measurement name like $cpu$.]
this tags's value is object type's icon file name that the scouter client have. eg)redis)input_telegraf_$measurement$_objName_base2Ù[This option is just a sample. Change $measurement$ to your measurement name like $cpu$.]
define an objectName prefix. objectName is defined with some tags.
see input_telegraf_$measurement$_objName_append_tags option.0input_telegraf_$measurement$_objName_append_tags2²[This option is just a sample. Change $measurement$ to your measurement name like $cpu$.]
this tags's value is appended to objName_base.
It can have multiple values. eg)tag1,tag2%input_telegraf_$measurement$_host_tag2q[This option is just a sample. Change $measurement$ to your measurement name like $cpu$.]
